<%#
  Hook 3 (render_plugin_partials): "basic_information_resource" is rendered
  just before the closing </fieldset> of the Basic Information section on
  the resource edit form and show page, i.e. after the built-in fields.
  Locals: :form, :record (see _top_of_basic_information_resource.html.erb
  for notes on what `form` is in each case).

  Unlike the alert box above, this partial is styled to match a real
  ArchivesSpace form field exactly -- the same "form-group w-100 row" /
  "control-label text-right col-sm-2" / "col-sm-9" markup ArchivesSpace's
  own form helpers generate (see label_with_field in aspace_form_helper.rb,
  which every label_and_* helper -- e.g. label_and_textfield -- calls under
  the hood).

  This is still just a display mockup, though: the input is disabled, and
  even if it weren't, this hook has no way to make ArchivesSpace persist
  whatever's typed into it -- it only controls where something gets drawn
  on the page. Adding a genuinely new, saved field requires real plugin
  work beyond the frontend: extending the schema, a migration, and usually
  an indexer change (see the `hello_world` plugin for that full pattern).
%>
<div class="form-group w-100 row">
  <label class="control-label text-right col-sm-2" for="plugin_hooks_example_level_display">
    plugin_hooks_example: Level, spelled out
  </label>
  <div class="col-sm-9">
    <input
      type="text"
      id="plugin_hooks_example_level_display"
      class="form-control"
      disabled
      value="<%= I18n.t("enumerations.archival_record_level.#{record['level']}", :default => record['level']) %>"
    />
    <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
      Disabled -- this field isn't real. Even enabled, this hook has no way
      to save what's typed here; that needs real backend plugin work.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
